  "details": "Let avatar creators upload optimized, bite-sized versions of avatars they've made to use in place of generated impostors. These \"manual impostors\" would be like fallbacks, but made specifically for an avatar that we personally made. Even better if the manual impostors are able to sync parameters with the main version of the avatar with what parameters they do have. This way, others can use your avatars and be seen without just the impostors I don't know the specific process, but here's a suggestion:\n\nIf you make a version of your avatar that meets fallback requirements, you get the option to merge it into another, less optimized avatar you've made to display as the impostor rather than to have one generated.",
